      "properties": {
        "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "## MiniMax H3 \u2014 TURBO 4-step (AMD RDNA4 / R9700)\n\n**Renders a 5.2 s 864\u00d7480 clip with synced audio in ~85 s** (encode cached).\n\n### Locked-in settings \u2014 change these two together or not at all\n- **Steps = 4** in `BasicScheduler`. This LoRA is *step-distilled*: it is trained\n  for the exact sigma schedule `[1.0, 0.973, 0.9231, 0.8, 0.0]`, whose single big\n  `0.8 \u2192 0.0` jump is the whole trick. **8 steps looks WORSE**, not better \u2014 it\n  inserts a `0.6316` point the LoRA has never seen. Do not \"improve\" this to 8.\n- **Turbo Sampler** is required. A plain `KSamplerSelect` will not work.\n\n### Dial for artifacting\n`MiniMaxH3TurboLoRA \u2192 strength`. The LoRA is slightly over-sharp by design\n(author's words: \"plastic-looking skin and over-sharp grain/noise\").\n- `1.00` sharpest, most grain\n- `0.85` noticeably cleaner\n- **`0.70` \u2190 set here.** Cleanest; below the author's stated 0.8\u20131.2 range, so\n  back off toward 0.85 if it ever looks soft or undercooked.\n\n### Resolution\n864\u00d7480 / 124 frames / 24 fps. Both dims are multiples of 32 (required).\nFrame count sits on H3's `17k+5` grid. Attention cost scales with the **square**\nof pixel count, so raising resolution gets expensive fast.\n\n### Launch with\n`Launch ComfyUI AMD RDNA4.bat` \u2014 it sets `--disable-smart-memory` and the\nInductor cache dir that the autotuned attention kernel needs. A new resolution\ncosts a one-time ~40 s kernel autotune, then it is cached forever.\n\n### Speed reference (864\u00d7480, 124f)\n| config | time |\n|---|---|\n| stock ComfyUI, 20 steps | 386 s |\n| patched, 20 steps | 272 s |\n| **patched + Turbo, 4 steps** | **~85 s** |\n"
      ]
    },
